# Auth & Session Patterns

## Session Model
*   Fields: `token`, `email`, `expirationDate`, `userId` (FK to users).
*   Token stored server-side; client sends it as Bearer header on each request.
*   Session TTL: 24 hours (`expiresIn: 86400` on JWT; matching `expirationDate` on row).
*   On login, reuse non-expired session for same user before issuing a new token.

## Login Response Payload
`POST /login` and `POST /dev-login` return flat JSON (not wrapped):
```json
{
  "userId": 1,
  "email": "jane.doe@eagles.oc.edu",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "roles": [{ "id": 3, "role": "area_admin", "areaId": 2, "area": { "id": 2, "name": "Athletics" } }],
  "token": "<jwt>"
}
```
There is no registration and no password sign-in: users come from Google sign-in only (Feature 3 FR-013). See `security.mdc`.

## Frontend Auth State
*   The signed-in user lives in the Pinia auth store, `useAuthStore()` (`stores/auth.js`). It is the only code that touches `localStorage`: it loads key `user` at startup and writes it back on every change, so sessions survive reloads.
*   Change it only through its actions: `signIn(res.data)` with the full login response, `signOut()`, `setRoles(roles)`. Read `user`, `isSignedIn`, `token`, `roles`. Never read or write `localStorage` `user` directly.
*   `authServices.js`: `loginUser`, `devLogin`, `logoutUser` methods calling `apiClient.post` (see `frontend-services.mdc`).
*   Logout clears the server session, then `useAuthStore().signOut()`, then routes to login.
*   `router.beforeEach`: routes with `meta.public` (login) are open without a session and send a signed-in user home; any other route without a session → login; then `meta.roles` via `canOpen()`.
*   Axios token attachment and 401 redirect: `frontend-services.mdc`.
*   Tests set the user with `signInAs(user)` / `signInAs(null)` from `tests/testUtils.js`, not `localStorage`.

## Role-aware UI
*   Role checks go through `useRoles()`:
    *   `hasAnyRole(roles)` — **access** decisions (route guards, nav links, action buttons). Admins always pass.
    *   `hasRole(role, areaId?)` — **display** only (chips, labels). Admins do not implicitly hold other roles here.
    *   `areaAdminAreaIds` — scope area-admin screens to the user's areas.
*   Never compare role strings in components (`user.roles.some(r => r.role === "admin")`); add a helper to `useRoles` if one is missing.
*   Roles refresh once per page load (`GET /api/users/:id` in the first `router.beforeEach`, Feature 3 FR-009). The UI can be stale until reload; the API is what enforces access, so every frontend check has a matching backend guard.
*   An action a user cannot take on themselves (removing their own admin role, deleting their own account) stays visible but **disabled**, with the reason shown — not hidden.

## Development-only UI
*   Gate developer tools in the UI on `import.meta.env.DEV` (production builds never render them) **and** back them with a server switch that is off by default (e.g. `DEV_LOGIN=true`, refused when `NODE_ENV=production`).
